; ==========================================================================
; STELLAR MAZE  -  VM2: solves it   (loads at $5000)   (web copy based at $4000: the Multitasking page moves program 2 to $5000 itself)
; ==========================================================================
; Load BOTH programs - Maze-VM1.lst at $4000 and Maze-VM2.lst at $5000 - then
; cold-boot and press a key. VM1 carves a random 25 x 10 maze on screen (a
; depth-first backtracker, multitasking OFF so it has the whole CPU). Then it
; copies the grid into VM2's memory with $DC COPYBVMXVMY and triggers VM2 by
; writing 1 into VM2's RB with $D3 COPYVXY. VM2 solves it right-hand-on-the-wall:
; 'o' is the path, '.' the dead ends it backed out of.
;
; VT100: cursor addressing and reverse video (the walls) only.
;
; VERIFICATION (Firmware-Math/maze_verify.py, V0061.33, two-VM cold boot): three mazes (the key pressed at three different moments) each read back off the screen as a PERFECT 25 x 10 maze equal to VM1's grid; VM2's copy has identical walls (all 1,196 bytes moved by $DC); the 'o' left on screen is exactly the start-to-exit path, '.' only off it, and the step and path counts match a Python right-hand walk. About 15.6 million 1802 instructions (~1.5 min at 3 MHz) + ~12 KB of output (~13 s at 9600 baud).
; NOT YET RUN ON HARDWARE.
;
; 137 STELLAR commands.
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

; D 5000 CD             START
; D 5001 11 0B 00 00    LOADXI R11 0000                    RB = 0: VM1 sets it to 1 when the maze is ours
; D 5005 D0 12          SHAREVM on, read/write             VM1 may write our memory and registers
; D 5007 11 0F 00 0A    LOADXI R15 000A
; D 500B 11 0C 00 34    LOADXI R12 0034
; WAIT:
; D 500F 86 0B 00 01    TESTXI R11 0001
; D 5013 A1 00 0F       IFFALSEI WAIT                      Wait for the trigger
; D 5016 11 0E 06 00    LOADXI R14 0600
; D 501A C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 501C 11 05 04 41    LOADXI R5 0441                     R5 = the bottom-right cell
; D 5020 11 02 00 69    LOADXI R2 0069                     R2 = where we are
; D 5024 11 03 00 02    LOADXI R3 0002                     R3 = heading: 0 up 1 right 2 down 3 left
; D 5028 10 00 6F       LOADAI 006F
; D 502B 2F 02 08 00    WRITEIDX R2 0800
; D 502F 11 0A 00 6F    LOADXI R10 006F
; D 5033 23 00 2B       COPYXY R2 -> R11
; D 5036 BD 01 21       CALL DRAW
; D 5039 11 08 00 01    LOADXI R8 0001                     R8 = path length (cells)
; D 503D 11 09 00 00    LOADXI R9 0000                     R9 = steps
; STEP:
; D 5041 87 25          TESTXY R2 = R5
; D 5043 A0 00 C3       IFTRUEI SOLVED
; D 5046 23 00 34       COPYXY R3 -> R4
; D 5049 42 04          INCX R4
; D 504B 86 04 00 04    TESTXI R4 0004
; D 504F A1 00 56       IFFALSEI TRY                       R4 = heading + 1: try RIGHT first
; D 5052 11 04 00 00    LOADXI R4 0000
; TRY:
; D 5056 BD 00 E8       CALL OFF                           R6 = the wall that way, R7 = the cell beyond
; D 5059 2E 06 08 00    READIDX R6 0800
; D 505D 81 00 23       TESTAI 0023
; D 5060 A1 00 71       IFFALSEI FOUND                     Open
; D 5063 8C 04          TESTXZ R4
; D 5065 A1 00 6C       IFFALSEI TL                        Blocked: turn left one
; D 5068 11 04 00 04    LOADXI R4 0004
; TL:
; D 506C 43 04          DECX R4
; D 506E B0 00 56       GAL TRY
; FOUND:
; D 5071 42 09          INCX R9
; D 5073 2E 07 08 00    READIDX R7 0800
; D 5077 81 00 6F       TESTAI 006F
; D 507A A0 00 9D       IFTRUEI BACK                       Stepping back onto the path
; D 507D 10 00 6F       LOADAI 006F
; D 5080 2F 06 08 00    WRITEIDX R6 0800
; D 5084 2F 07 08 00    WRITEIDX R7 0800
; D 5088 11 0A 00 6F    LOADXI R10 006F
; D 508C 23 00 6B       COPYXY R6 -> R11
; D 508F BD 01 21       CALL DRAW
; D 5092 23 00 7B       COPYXY R7 -> R11
; D 5095 BD 01 21       CALL DRAW
; D 5098 42 08          INCX R8
; D 509A B0 00 BA       GAL MOVED
; BACK:
; D 509D 10 00 2E       LOADAI 002E
; D 50A0 2F 02 08 00    WRITEIDX R2 0800
; D 50A4 2F 06 08 00    WRITEIDX R6 0800
; D 50A8 11 0A 00 2E    LOADXI R10 002E
; D 50AC 23 00 2B       COPYXY R2 -> R11
; D 50AF BD 01 21       CALL DRAW
; D 50B2 23 00 6B       COPYXY R6 -> R11
; D 50B5 BD 01 21       CALL DRAW
; D 50B8 43 08          DECX R8
; MOVED:
; D 50BA 23 00 72       COPYXY R7 -> R2
; D 50BD 23 00 43       COPYXY R4 -> R3
; D 50C0 B0 00 41       GAL STEP
; SOLVED:
; D 50C3 23 00 87       COPYXY R8 -> R7                    Path length out of R8: PRNUM counts digits in R8
; D 50C6 11 0E 06 39    LOADXI R14 0639
; D 50CA C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 50CC 23 00 94       COPYXY R9 -> R4
; D 50CF BD 01 5B       CALL PRNUM
; D 50D2 11 0E 06 51    LOADXI R14 0651
; D 50D6 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 50D8 23 00 74       COPYXY R7 -> R4
; D 50DB BD 01 5B       CALL PRNUM
; D 50DE 11 0E 06 67    LOADXI R14 0667
; D 50E2 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 50E4 00             HALT
; D 50E5 F0 00 00       BREAK
; OFF:
; D 50E8 23 00 26       COPYXY R2 -> R6
; D 50EB 86 04 00 00    TESTXI R4 0000
; D 50EF A0 01 07       IFTRUEI OU
; D 50F2 86 04 00 01    TESTXI R4 0001
; D 50F6 A0 01 0E       IFTRUEI OR
; D 50F9 86 04 00 02    TESTXI R4 0002
; D 50FD A0 01 15       IFTRUEI OD
; D 5100 53 06 00 01    SUBXI R6 0001                      left
; D 5104 B0 01 19       GAL ON
; OU:
; D 5107 53 06 00 34    SUBXI R6 0034
; D 510B B0 01 19       GAL ON
; OR:
; D 510E 52 06 00 01    ADDXI R6 0001
; D 5112 B0 01 19       GAL ON
; OD:
; D 5115 52 06 00 34    ADDXI R6 0034
; ON:
; D 5119 50 66 07       ADDXYZ R6 + R6 -> R7
; D 511C 51 72 07       SUBXYZ R7 - R2 -> R7               next = 2 x wall - here
; D 511F BE 00          RETURN
; DRAW:
; D 5121 4D BC          DIVXY R11 / R12                    row + 1, column
; D 5123 25             COPYMAA
; D 5124 21 0D          COPYAX Acc -> R13
; D 5126 52 0D 00 02    ADDXI R13 0002
; D 512A 27             COPYREMA
; D 512B 21 0E          COPYAX Acc -> R14
; D 512D 52 0E 00 0F    ADDXI R14 000F
; D 5131 BD 01 39       CALL POSXY
; D 5134 22 0A          COPYXA R10 -> Acc
; D 5136 C9             SEROUT
; D 5137 BE 00          RETURN
; POSXY:
; D 5139 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B
; D 513B CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B '['
; D 513D 4D DF          DIVXY R13 / R15
; D 513F 25             COPYMAA
; D 5140 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 5143 C9             SEROUT
; D 5144 27             COPYREMA
; D 5145 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 5148 C9             SEROUT
; D 5149 CA 3B          SEROUTI 3B ';'
; D 514B 4D EF          DIVXY R14 / R15
; D 514D 25             COPYMAA
; D 514E 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 5151 C9             SEROUT
; D 5152 27             COPYREMA
; D 5153 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 5156 C9             SEROUT
; D 5157 CA 48          SEROUTI 48 'H'
; D 5159 BE 00          RETURN
; PRNUM:
; D 515B 11 08 00 00    LOADXI R8 0000
; PN1:
; D 515F 4D 4F          DIVXY R4 / R15
; D 5161 27             COPYREMA
; D 5162 70 00          PUSHA Acc                          digits onto the stack
; D 5164 42 08          INCX R8
; D 5166 25             COPYMAA
; D 5167 21 04          COPYAX Acc -> R4
; D 5169 8C 04          TESTXZ R4
; D 516B A1 01 5F       IFFALSEI PN1
; PN2:
; D 516E 71 00          POPA Acc
; D 5170 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 5173 C9             SEROUT
; D 5174 43 08          DECX R8
; D 5176 8C 08          TESTXZ R8
; D 5178 A1 01 6E       IFFALSEI PN2
; D 517B BE 00          RETURN

